      "text": "You didn't even visit the National Palace Museum in Taiwan? You might not know that when the Kuomintang (KMT) was losing the war against the Communists in China, they retreated from various cities, taking all these precious ancient Chinese artifacts with them. In fact, the artifacts were taken away even earlier than the equipment and food. Although they eventually lost to the Communists and came to Taiwan, they brought the most valuable Chinese artifacts to Taiwan. Even though the KMT regime was very poor when they came to Taiwan, they still spent a lot of money to preserve the artifacts. As a result, if you want to see the most valuable Chinese artifacts now, you can basically only see them in Taiwan.",
